# W44-183 HONEST-STOP — CfL Newton libjxl-parity port REGRESSES on every cell
# Date: 2026-05-22
# Cells: 9 images x 3 distances = 27 cells (5 CID22 photos + 3 GB82-SC screens + clic_097cb426)
# Effort: e7 (Newton gate fires at speed_tier <= kSquirrel)
# Status: RULED OUT — fix abandoned, ZERO production code change shipped
#
# ── Background ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# W44-178 → W44-181 → W44-182 chain (commits 1a2d1ee70c0f → 524e2159 → 3c2026b2):
# clic_097cb426 e7 d=5 has a right-column SSIM2 deficit of -7 vs cjxl. W44-178
# falsified the DCT64X64 IDCT/dequant/CfL/EPF/gaborish hypothesis (right column
# has the SMALLEST per-pixel diff in the image despite the -7 SSIM2 — sub-pixel
# shift on smooth content). W44-181 falsified DC quant precision drift (0/13873
# divergences). W44-182 found that find_best_multiplier_newton diverges from
# libjxl in 4 parameters:
#
#     | param         | ours       | libjxl |
#     |---            |---         |---     |
#     | eps           | 1.0        | 100    |
#     | max_iters     | 10         | 20     |
#     | starting x    | ls_x       | 0      |
#     | non-converge  | fall to ls | last x |
#
# AND on the W44-182 cmap dump, ours produced ytox=0 for ALL 256 tiles while
# cjxl produced 134/256 nonzero (pass 2). The right column tx=15 had the
# highest |Δytox| 4.68-6.04 per tile, matching the -7 SSIM2 zone.
#
# W44-182's hypothesis: porting libjxl's 4 parameters bit-exactly would close
# the SSIM2 deficit. W44-183 (this chunk) tested that hypothesis.
#
# ── Method ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Wrote the W44-183 fix at jxl-encoder-simd/src/cfl.rs:
#    - NEWTON_EPS_DEFAULT: 1.0 → 100.0
#    - NEWTON_MAX_ITERS_DEFAULT: 10 → 20
#    - Removed LS warm-start; start Newton at x = 0
#    - Removed LS fallback; use last x regardless of convergence
#    Applied to all 3 paths (scalar, AVX2, NEON).
#
# 2. Re-ran W44-182 probe — confirmed right-column tx=15 now BYTE-EXACT to cjxl
#    (every one of 16 ty positions matches exactly):
#       ty | ours(ytox,ytob) | cjxl(ytox,ytob)
#        0 | ( +5,   -4)    | ( +5,   -4)   <- bit-exact
#        1 | ( +4,  -11)    | ( +4,  -11)   <- bit-exact
#       ...
#       15 | ( +6,  -14)    | ( +6,  -14)   <- bit-exact
#
# 3. Re-ran W44-178 region_ssim2 — STILL -7.0/-7.7/-7.4 right-column SSIM2.
#    The CfL fix did NOT close the SSIM2 deficit.
#
# 4. Spot-check on 9 images × 3 distances (this TSV): the fix REGRESSED 25/27
#    cells with a mean +7.82% byte overhead. Worst cases:
#       cid22_1531677 d=5: SSIM2 -13.02, bytes +26.4%
#       cid22_1420710 d=5: SSIM2 -11.92, bytes +12.9%
#       cid22_1531677 d=3: SSIM2 -10.46, bytes +16.5%
#       cid22_1418519 d=5: SSIM2  -6.35, bytes  +5.7%
#
# ── Decision: HONEST-STOP, REVERT ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Per the W44-183 task spec ("Fix produces large regressions on other corpus
# images → ANALYZE before reverting"):
#
# The W44-183 production code change has been REVERTED. The committed artefacts
# document the falsification:
#
#   benchmarks/w44_183_cfl_newton_spotcheck_2026-05-22.pre.tsv  (W44-182 baseline)
#   benchmarks/w44_183_cfl_newton_spotcheck_2026-05-22.post.tsv (W44-183 fix)
#   jxl-encoder/examples/w44_183_cfl_newton_spotcheck.rs        (reproducer)
#
# ── Root-cause analysis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The W44-178 → W44-182 chain mis-attributed the SSIM2 deficit to CfL Newton.
# CfL Newton IS a measurable divergence vs libjxl (W44-182 verified the cmap
# dump shows 0/256 nonzero on ours vs 134/256 cjxl pre-fix; bit-exact match on
# right column post-fix). But fixing Newton to libjxl parity:
#
#   1. Does NOT close the right-column SSIM2 deficit (W44-178 region SSIM2
#      unchanged at -7.0/-7.7/-7.4).
#   2. CAUSES a categorical SSIM2 regression on every other image tested
#      (25/27 cells worse, 0 cells better).
#
# Why does libjxl-parity Newton REGRESS our pipeline?  Likely cause: the rest of
# our encoder (quant decisions, AC strategy selection, butteraugli loop seeds,
# adaptive_quant, entropy_mul tables) has been incrementally tuned over W44-29
# through W44-172 against the broken CfL-Newton baseline (which converged to
# ls_x via the warm-start + low-eps + fallback path, effectively producing
# LS solutions almost everywhere). Suddenly producing libjxl-correct ytox/ytob
# multipliers throws off the downstream calibration. This is the same class of
# integrated-pipeline-divergence that W44-86 / W44-87 / W44-90 / W44-95
# hit when trying isolated lever changes.
#
# Cardinal-rule "leave nothing unported" tension: there IS a divergence here,
# but porting it regresses real-world quality. The right move is to ship the
# falsification (this memo + TSVs) so future agents do NOT re-attempt a naive
# port. Future work should either (a) tackle the downstream calibration that
# compensates for the broken CfL Newton, or (b) find the actual root cause of
# the clic_097cb426 right-column SSIM2 deficit (a fourth candidate after
# W44-178/181/182 all falsified).
#
# ── Hard acceptance gates: all FAILED ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# (a) Build PASS               YES — fix compiles cleanly
# (b) cargo test --lib         PASS (1825/1825) with the fix
# (c) Hash-locks                Would regen 22 lossy fixtures (32 → 1825 tests
#                               pass after regen) — REVERTED, byte-identical to
#                               pre-W44-183 baseline.
# (d) clic_097cb426 right-col SSIM2 <= -1.0: FAILED (stays at -7.0)
# (e) clic_097cb426 overall SSIM2 <= -1.0:   FAILED (stays at -3 to -4.5)
# (f) Other cells within +-5% bytes / +-0.30 SSIM2: FAILED (mean +7.82% bytes,
