#     drifted, ONE (32x32_d1) stayed at same size but with different hash
# (i) Multi-decoder PASS:       YES — fixed output decodes cleanly via
#                               jxl-rs/jxl-oxide/djxl. The output is VALID; it
#                               just measures worse.
#
# ── DO NOT (future agents) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# - DO NOT re-attempt the bit-exact libjxl Newton parameter port at the
#   DEFAULT path. Measurement (this TSV) is conclusive: 0/27 SSIM2 wins,
#   25/27 SSIM2 regressions.
# - DO NOT cite "CfL Newton" as the cause of the clic_097cb426 right-column
#   SSIM2 deficit (W44-173/177/178/181/182 are all FALSIFIED).
# - DO consider porting libjxl-correct Newton ONLY under EncoderStrategy::Libjxl
#   (where all-libjxl-parity is the contract and bytes/SSIM2 changes are
#   expected). That would require updating LIBJXL_PINS sizes and adding a
#   per-EncoderStrategy gate on NEWTON_EPS_DEFAULT.
# - DO investigate other root causes for the clic_097cb426 deficit. The W44-178
#   per-pixel diff is tiny (0.008 max-abs RGB) but the SSIM2 amplification is
#   -7 — investigate sub-pixel-shift amplification, low-frequency DC stability,
